{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "82cb6702-2da8-8a07-8f84-3c8f9fa21439",
  "created_at": "2026-02-04T12:46:19-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Diego Valdez",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Owen Haskell",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:41:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, this is Owen. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:41:59-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, yes. Good afternoon. I am calling about a certificate? My, um, my daughter's birth certificate. The name is spelled wrong."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:42:08-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Sorry to hear that. Let's go slowly. Is that a birth certificate from Newport, so she was born here?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:42:16-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, born in Newport. At the hospital. Two years ago. They wrote her middle name with one letter missing. I want to make it correct? Can I get a new one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:42:28-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. So that's what's called a correction, or an amendment. It isn't quite a new copy, the record itself gets changed. I'll tell you the general steps, and you can write them down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:42:41-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, okay. Sorry, I am on the speaker phone. Is it okay? You can hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:42:48-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. A little echo, but fine. So, usually you fill out a form for the correction and you bring something that shows the right spelling. Something like the hospital paperwork, or a baptismal record, whatever was made close to the birth."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:05-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The hospital paper. I have a paper they gave us when we left. It has the name correct, I think. The certificate is wrong, the paper is right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:16-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could help. Bring it along. Now, you'll also need to show who you are. Are you one of the parents listed on the certificate?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:26-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I am the father. My name is on it. Diego Valdez."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:31-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Then you'd bring a photo ID, like a driver's license or a passport. Something government issued, not expired."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Driver's license, okay. Only one? Or also the passport? I have both."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:44-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, and what about my wife? She must come also?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:43:49-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One parent can usually start it. Bring the one ID, the license is fine. If the other parent is needed for a signature, we'll tell you when you come in. I'd say bring her ID too, just in case, if it's easy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:05-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. Both ID. I understand."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:08-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Now, there's a record number on the certificate, it's near the top. If you have it in front of you, I can note it and have the file pulled before you come."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, let me find. [pause] Yes. I have it. It is two, zero, two, four, dash, zero, four, one, seven, eight, nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:30-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, let me read that back. Two zero two four, dash, zero four one seven eight nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:37-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Okay, I will say again to be sure. Two zero two four, dash, zero, one, four, seven, eight, nine?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:45-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Close, but not quite. You said zero four one seven eight nine the first time. The four comes before the one. Zero, four, one, seven, eight, nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:44:56-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, sorry. Zero, four, one, seven, eight, nine. Yes. I switched them. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:02-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, that's why we read them back. I've got it written down now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:08-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I come to City Hall? Any time? Or I need appointment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:13-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can walk in during office hours, Monday through Friday. Mornings tend to be a little quieter. It's better to come with everything together, the hospital paper and the IDs."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:25-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And the, um, the new certificate, it will be ready the same day? Or I wait?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:32-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't promise same day. The correction can take some time to process, and the state may need to review it. The person at the counter will tell you more when you bring the form in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:46-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So first the correction, and then I ask for the copy? Two steps?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:52-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the usual order, yes. Correction first, then a copy of the corrected record."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:45:58-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I think I understand. Maybe. I will bring the hospital paper, license, my wife license, and the number. Zero four one seven eight nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:46:08-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. You've got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:46:11-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much. Sorry for my English."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T12:46:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Your English is fine. Take care, Mr. Valdez."
    }
  ],
